Following a word ending in an [[alveolar]] [[obstruent]] ({{IPAchar|/t/}}, {{IPAchar|/d/}}, {{IPAchar|/s/}}{{,}} or {{IPAchar|/z/}}), the words may coalesce and [[palatalize]], resulting in [[postalveolar]] {{IPAchar|/tʃ/}}, {{IPAchar|/dʒ/}}, {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}}{{,}} and {{IPAchar|/ʒ/}}, respectively. This is occasionally represented in writing, for example {{m|en|gotcha}} (from {{m|en|[[got]] [[you]]}}) or {{m|en|[[whatcha]] [[doin']]}} (more formally {{m|en|[[what]] [[are]] [[you]] [[doing]]?}}).

